# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) checked files out as
# CRLF, so Prettier — which emits LF — reported 71 files as "unformatted" while
# containing no real style drift. That permanently kept `yarn format:check` red and
# made every Windows edit look like a whole-file change.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in git and checks out the platform-native ending locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows, or bash fails with a shebang error.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never attempt text conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Prettier and lockfiles: exact bytes matter for diffs.
yarn.lock text eol=lf
